# ============================================================
#  Club and job spells (spells v2, docs/spells-v2-list.md §G).
#  Every chain has the same shape:
#   - a start card, pushed once you reach the track's second rank (and again later if you turn it down): it sets
#     <spell>_chain and leaves a lead;
#   - three preparation cards, each a check or a resource spent, each leaving a flag (skipped, they come back);
#   - the final milestone check on the spell's skill (once two preparations are done and a month has passed, or four
#     months on), one step
#     easier per preparation done (`even` plus three steps is
#     near certain), with a paid route at better odds for the underprepared. On a loss it comes back later, and the
#     preparation is kept.
#  Measured 2026-10-17: a club meets about twice a term and a track pool is ~20 cards, so with §G's weight ~8 for a
#  drawn start card most rank-2 members never saw the chain. The start is pushed instead, and the chain's cards
#  outweigh the pool while it runs (preparation 60, final 40).
#  Two beats a visit (feedback 2026-10-19, migration 0035): the start's accepting option queues the first preparation
#  `now`, and a preparation's working option queues, once a visit (`chain_beat`), the final when it is ready or else
#  the next preparation not done. Measured over 90 games: learned 60% of chains started (was 43%), median 6 months
#  from start to spell (was 8).
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Duelling Circle → Brace (vigor) ----------------

@event duel_dummy_hexes
title: The Dummy Hits Back
track: duelling
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: rank(duelling) >= 2 and spell_level(brace) == 0 and not flag(brace_chain) and turn <= 44
repeat: 3
art: shield
tags: club duel
scene: A duel hall's practice corner, an eyepatched straw dummy flinging a crackling hex back at a startled student, stuffing spilling from a split seam.
text: The eyepatched dummy has started throwing hexes back. Lyra splits its seam and pulls out an old captain's charm, sewn in decades ago and still humming. "It empties if someone holds firm in the circle while it fires," she says. "Nobody's managed it. Nobody's tried properly."
> left: "I'll try properly."
  flag brace_chain
  find lead_brace
  perform duelling +tiny
  say: Lyra sews the charm back in, looks at you, and writes your name on the board under the dummy. Underneath, someone adds a small drawing of a stretcher.
  chain_beat = turn
  queue duel_captains_notes now
> right: Leave it to the seniors
  mood +tiny
  say: You go back to your bout, and the dummy goes back to hexing whoever passes. A senior limps past at the end of practice, still smoking slightly.

@event duel_captains_notes
title: The Captain's Notes
track: duelling
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(brace_chain) and not flag(brace_notes) and spell_level(brace) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: scroll
tags: club study
scene: A dusty cupboard in the duel hall, a student reading a cracked leather notebook by the light of a single lamp.
text: The captain who made the charm left notes, in a cupboard under the trophy shelf, in a hand like barbed wire. Half of it is about footwork and the other half is insults addressed to people long graduated.
> left: Read them properly
  challenge research journeyman:
    win:
      flag brace_notes
      lore +small
      say: Between the insults is the trick: you don't stop the first blow, you let it land on something that isn't you. You copy the page out and put the notebook back where the captain would have wanted it.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: You read until the lamp gutters and learn a great deal about a student called Pim, who could not parry. The trick is in there somewhere. You'll have to come back for it.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(duel_dummy_hexes) >= 1 and flag(brace_notes) + flag(brace_circle) + flag(brace_footwork) >= 2:
      queue duel_brace_final now
    elif not flag(brace_circle):
      queue duel_bram_barrage now
    elif not flag(brace_footwork):
      queue duel_footwork_lyra now
> right: Spar instead tonight
  perform duelling +small
  say: You leave the notes for another evening and take a bout instead. You win it, which is the other kind of useful.

@event duel_bram_barrage
title: Inside the Chalk Circle
track: duelling
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: tense
when: flag(brace_chain) and not flag(brace_circle) and spell_level(brace) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: bolt
tags: club duel
scene: A student standing in a chalk circle on a scorched floor while a broad prefect hurls a stream of stinging hexes from the edge.
text: Word reaches Bram that you mean to empty the captain's charm. He turns up with his sleeves rolled. "Regulation hazing," he announces, "section four. You stand in the circle. I throw. You don't step out. Ready?"
> left: Hold the circle against him
  challenge feat vs bram.vigor:
    win:
      flag brace_circle
      vigor +small
      say: You don't step out. By the twentieth hex Bram is red in the face and you are still in the circle, scorched and planted. "Adequate," he says, gruffly, and doesn't put you on report.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: The ninth hex knocks you clean out of the circle. Bram notes it in his book. "Section four, failed," he says. "Again next week."
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(duel_dummy_hexes) >= 1 and flag(brace_notes) + flag(brace_circle) + flag(brace_footwork) >= 2:
      queue duel_brace_final now
    elif not flag(brace_notes):
      queue duel_captains_notes now
    elif not flag(brace_footwork):
      queue duel_footwork_lyra now
> right: Take it all on your shield arm
  flag brace_circle
  health -medium
  say: You don't try to be clever. You just stand there and take it, every hex, on your arm, until Bram runs out. Your arm is purple for a week. Bram looks almost impressed.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(duel_dummy_hexes) >= 1 and flag(brace_notes) + flag(brace_circle) + flag(brace_footwork) >= 2:
      queue duel_brace_final now
    elif not flag(brace_notes):
      queue duel_captains_notes now
    elif not flag(brace_footwork):
      queue duel_footwork_lyra now
> up[item:duelling_coat]: Shrug it off in the coat
  flag brace_circle
  health -small
  perform duelling +tiny
  say: You button the quilted coat to the chin and plant your feet. The hexes thud into the padding like snowballs into a wall. Bram runs out first. "That's cheating," he says. "Section four doesn't mention coats," you say.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(duel_dummy_hexes) >= 1 and flag(brace_notes) + flag(brace_circle) + flag(brace_footwork) >= 2:
      queue duel_brace_final now
    elif not flag(brace_notes):
      queue duel_captains_notes now
    elif not flag(brace_footwork):
      queue duel_footwork_lyra now

@event duel_footwork_lyra
title: Footwork Until Dark
track: duelling
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(brace_chain) and not flag(brace_footwork) and spell_level(brace) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: wand
tags: club duel
scene: An empty duel hall at dusk, two students drilling footwork across chalk marks, one of them pointing sharply at the other's feet.
text: Lyra finds you after practice. "The captain's notes say the stance is everything," she says. "Your stance is a disgrace. Three hours. Now." She has already chalked the marks on the floor.
> left: Drill until dark
  flag brace_footwork
  mood -small
  rel lyra +tiny
  say: She is merciless and exact. By dark you can set your feet without thinking, and you never want to see a chalk mark again. "Better," she says, which from Lyra is a sonnet.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(duel_dummy_hexes) >= 1 and flag(brace_notes) + flag(brace_circle) + flag(brace_footwork) >= 2:
      queue duel_brace_final now
    elif not flag(brace_notes):
      queue duel_captains_notes now
    elif not flag(brace_circle):
      queue duel_bram_barrage now
> right: "Tomorrow. I have an essay."
  study +tiny
  rel lyra -tiny
  say: She looks at you as if you'd chosen to lose. You write the essay. It is a fine essay, and Lyra mentions your stance at breakfast.

@event duel_brace_final
title: Hold Firm
track: duelling
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: tense
when: flag(brace_chain) and spell_level(brace) == 0 and since(duel_dummy_hexes) >= 1 and (flag(brace_notes) + flag(brace_circle) + flag(brace_footwork) >= 2 or since(duel_dummy_hexes) >= 4)
repeat: 2
weight: 40
art: spell_brace
tags: club duel magic
scene: A student standing firm in a chalk circle in a crowded duel hall as an eyepatched dummy fires hex after hex, the club watching from the benches.
text: The club gathers on the benches. You step into the chalk circle, and the eyepatched dummy turns its head toward you with an audible creak. The captain's charm begins to fire. {flag(brace_notes) and flag(brace_circle) and flag(brace_footwork): You know how to stand, and why.|You have done some of the work. Not all of it.}
> left: Hold firm
  challenge feat adept- +1 if flag(brace_notes) +1 if flag(brace_circle) +1 if flag(brace_footwork):
    win:
      learn_spell brace
      perform duelling +small
      say: The hexes break on you one after another, and each lands softer than the last. When the charm finally sputters out, the club is on its feet. Lyra doesn't clap. She nods, once, which is louder.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: The fourteenth hex lifts you out of the circle and into the benches. The dummy turns its head back with a creak. It will be there at practice, waiting.
> right: Borrow the captain's old gauntlets
  gold -small
  challenge feat adept- likely +1 if flag(brace_notes) +1 if flag(brace_circle) +1 if flag(brace_footwork):
    win:
      learn_spell brace
      perform duelling +small
      say: The club quartermaster rents you the captain's own gauntlets for the night. They take the first blow for you, and the rest you take yourself. When the charm sputters out, the benches roar.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: Even in the gauntlets, the fourteenth hex lifts you out of the circle. The rental is not refunded. The dummy creaks its head back and waits.

# ---------------- The Lumen Ledger → Quickquill (guile) ----------------

@event ledger_spare_quill
title: The Spare Quill
track: lumen_ledger
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: rank(lumen_ledger) >= 2 and spell_level(quickquill) == 0 and not flag(quickquill_chain) and turn <= 44
repeat: 3
art: paper
tags: club
scene: A newspaper office with proofs pegged on a drying line, a lone quill hanging among them scribbling on a proof by itself.
text: A spare quill on the drying line has been finishing your sentences. Today it started inventing them: your proof now says the refectory serves dragon. "Oh, it's woken up," says Nessa, delighted. "Tame it and it's yours. Nobody's tamed one since I've been editor."
> left: Take the quill home
  flag quickquill_chain
  find lead_quickquill
  perform lumen_ledger +tiny
  say: You wrap it in a handkerchief. It writes "kidnapped" on the handkerchief. Nessa writes your name on the office board under QUILL, with a question mark.
  chain_beat = turn
  queue ledger_soup_complaint now
> right: Peg it back on the line
  mood +tiny
  say: You peg it back. It writes a small, hurt editorial about you on the next proof, which Nessa cuts, laughing.

@event ledger_soup_complaint
title: The Soup Complaint
track: lumen_ledger
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(quickquill_chain) and not flag(quickquill_soup) and spell_level(quickquill) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: letter
tags: club
scene: A desk buried in angry letters about soup, a student dictating firmly to a quill that keeps trying to add flourishes.
text: Forty furious letters about the refectory soup have arrived. Nessa wants one calm reply, printed. You decide to dictate it to the quill, which wants very badly to make it more exciting.
> left: Keep the quill to the facts
  challenge spell using guile journeyman:
    win:
      flag quickquill_soup
      guile +small
      say: Every time it reaches for a flourish, you catch it. The reply comes out calm, true and very dull. Nessa prints it. The quill sulks, and then, grudgingly, writes the next one straight.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: You blink and the quill has written that the soup contains a mild curse. It prints. You spend Thursday apologising to the cooks.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(ledger_spare_quill) >= 1 and flag(quickquill_soup) + flag(quickquill_ink) + flag(quickquill_deadline) >= 2:
      queue ledger_quill_interview now
    elif not flag(quickquill_ink):
      queue ledger_proper_ink now
    elif not flag(quickquill_deadline):
      queue ledger_deadline_night now
> right: Write the reply by hand
  perform lumen_ledger +tiny
  say: You write it yourself, slowly. It's a good reply. The quill watches from the inkwell, offended at being left out.

@event ledger_proper_ink
title: Proper Ink
track: lumen_ledger
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(quickquill_chain) and not flag(quickquill_ink) and spell_level(quickquill) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: coin
tags: club
scene: A stationer's counter in the village, a student holding a small dark bottle of ink up to the light while a quill pokes out of their pocket.
text: The quill refuses the school ink. It blots, it sulks, it writes "no" in large letters. The stationer in the village has proper ink, black as a well and priced like it.
> left: Buy the proper ink
  gold -small
  flag quickquill_ink
  say: The quill drinks the new ink and writes a whole page of your notes, neatly, in a better hand than yours. It underlines the bits you'll need. You feel slightly managed.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(ledger_spare_quill) >= 1 and flag(quickquill_soup) + flag(quickquill_ink) + flag(quickquill_deadline) >= 2:
      queue ledger_quill_interview now
    elif not flag(quickquill_soup):
      queue ledger_soup_complaint now
    elif not flag(quickquill_deadline):
      queue ledger_deadline_night now
> right: Make it use the school ink
  mood -tiny
  say: It uses the school ink under protest and blots every third word, including, pointedly, your name.

@event ledger_deadline_night
title: Deadline Night
track: lumen_ledger
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: tense
when: flag(quickquill_chain) and not flag(quickquill_deadline) and spell_level(quickquill) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: candle
tags: club
scene: A newspaper office after midnight, cold tea and candle stubs everywhere, a student and a quill working side by side while an editor paces.
text: Deadline night. The front page fell through at nine and Nessa is pacing. "We need eight hundred words by four," she says. "Anybody with a quill that writes fast, now is the time."
> left: Sit it out with the quill
  flag quickquill_deadline
  perform lumen_ledger +small
  mood -medium
  say: You and the quill write until four. By the end it finishes your sentences only when you want it to. You are both too tired to argue. Nessa puts your name on the page, small.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(ledger_spare_quill) >= 1 and flag(quickquill_soup) + flag(quickquill_ink) + flag(quickquill_deadline) >= 2:
      queue ledger_quill_interview now
    elif not flag(quickquill_soup):
      queue ledger_soup_complaint now
    elif not flag(quickquill_ink):
      queue ledger_proper_ink now
> right: Go to bed
  health +tiny
  say: You sleep. In the morning the front page is late and Nessa is hoarse, and the quill has written a bitter little poem about you on the pillowcase.

@event ledger_quill_interview
title: Deny Everything
track: lumen_ledger
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: tense
when: flag(quickquill_chain) and spell_level(quickquill) == 0 and since(ledger_spare_quill) >= 1 and (flag(quickquill_soup) + flag(quickquill_ink) + flag(quickquill_deadline) >= 2 or since(ledger_spare_quill) >= 4)
repeat: 2
weight: 40
art: spell_quickquill
tags: club magic
scene: A stuffy committee room, a smooth official smiling across a table at a student whose quill writes furiously on its own.
text: Nessa sends you to interview the chair of the refectory committee, who will deny everything, including the soup. "Get it word for word," she says. "Every word. They'll deny the words too." {flag(quickquill_soup) and flag(quickquill_ink) and flag(quickquill_deadline): Your quill sits up in your pocket, ready.|Your quill is half-tamed at best.}
> left: Interview them with the quill
  challenge negotiate using guile adept- +1 if flag(quickquill_soup) +1 if flag(quickquill_ink) +1 if flag(quickquill_deadline):
    win:
      learn_spell quickquill
      perform lumen_ledger +small
      say: The chair denies everything, and the quill takes every denial down word for word, including the one that contradicts the other three. Nessa reads it and goes very quiet. "Front page," she says.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: The quill gets bored halfway and starts improving the chair's answers. Nothing is printable. The quill sulks in the WILL NOT PRINT basket until your next front page.
> right: Prepare all night first
  mood -small
  challenge negotiate using guile adept- likely +1 if flag(quickquill_soup) +1 if flag(quickquill_ink) +1 if flag(quickquill_deadline):
    win:
      learn_spell quickquill
      perform lumen_ledger +small
      say: You go in tired and over-prepared, with every question written out. The quill follows your lead all the way through. Nessa reads the transcript twice. "Front page."
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: All night's preparation, and the chair simply doesn't turn up. The quill sulks in the WILL NOT PRINT basket until your next front page.

# ---------------- Verdant Circle → Bramble (alchemy) ----------------

@event verdant_far_bed
title: The Far Bed Answers
track: verdant
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: rank(verdant) >= 2 and spell_level(bramble) == 0 and not flag(bramble_chain) and turn <= 44
repeat: 3
art: leaf
tags: club nature
scene: The far end of a greenhouse, a tangle of vines reaching toward a student who has just found a green shoot curling out of their coat pocket.
text: The far bed answers back today: every vine in it turns to follow you. On the way out you find a seed in your coat pocket that wasn't there this morning, and it has already put out a shoot.
> left: Keep it and grow it
  flag bramble_chain
  find lead_bramble
  alchemy +tiny
  say: You cup it in your palm. The shoot curls round your finger, firmly. Tobias, when you show him, goes pale and then delighted. "That's a hedge-seed," he says. "They choose people."
  chain_beat = turn
  queue verdant_plant_seed now
> right: Give it to Tobias
  rel tobias +tiny
  say: Tobias takes it gently and puts it in a pot by the door. "It'll want you back," he says. "They usually do."

@event verdant_plant_seed
title: Somewhere to Grow
track: verdant
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: warm
when: flag(bramble_chain) and not flag(bramble_planted) and spell_level(bramble) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: leaf
tags: club nature
scene: Two students kneeling in a greenhouse bed planting a seedling, a lantern between them and earth up to their elbows.
text: The seed has outgrown your pocket. It needs a bed. Tobias offers the corner of his own in the greenhouse. Old Maud, passing, says there's a corner in her garden that never gets frost, "if you can keep a secret, dearie."
> left: Plant it with Tobias
  flag bramble_planted
  rel tobias +small
  say: You plant it together by lantern light, and Tobias tells it a long story about a goat to help it settle. It settles. So does Tobias, eventually.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(verdant_far_bed) >= 1 and flag(bramble_planted) + flag(bramble_fed) + flag(bramble_choir) >= 2:
      queue verdant_bramble_bolts now
    elif not flag(bramble_fed):
      queue verdant_cold_snap now
    elif not flag(bramble_choir):
      queue verdant_mandrake_choir now
> right: Plant it in Maud's garden
  flag bramble_planted
  rel maud +small
  say: Maud leads you through a door you'd never noticed into a garden you'll never find on your own. You plant it there. "It'll be happy," she says, "for a while."
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(verdant_far_bed) >= 1 and flag(bramble_planted) + flag(bramble_fed) + flag(bramble_choir) >= 2:
      queue verdant_bramble_bolts now
    elif not flag(bramble_fed):
      queue verdant_cold_snap now
    elif not flag(bramble_choir):
      queue verdant_mandrake_choir now

@event verdant_cold_snap
time: night
title: The Cold Snap
track: verdant
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: tense
when: flag(bramble_planted) and not flag(bramble_fed) and spell_level(bramble) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: snow
tags: club nature
scene: Frost creeping over a greenhouse bed at night, a student wrapped in a blanket sitting beside a shivering seedling with a lantern.
text: A hard frost is coming tonight, the first of the season. Your seedling is too young for it. Somebody would have to sit with it till dawn, feeding it warmth.
> left: Sit up with it all night
  flag bramble_fed
  health -small
  say: You sit wrapped round the lantern till dawn, feeding it what warmth you have. By morning you're stiff and coughing, and the seedling has grown a thorn, which it seems proud of.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(verdant_far_bed) >= 1 and flag(bramble_planted) + flag(bramble_fed) + flag(bramble_choir) >= 2:
      queue verdant_bramble_bolts now
    elif not flag(bramble_planted):
      queue verdant_plant_seed now
    elif not flag(bramble_choir):
      queue verdant_mandrake_choir now
> right: Cover it and hope
  mood -tiny
  say: You cover it with sacking and go to bed. It survives, sulking, and loses a leaf. It is noticeably cooler towards you.

@event verdant_mandrake_choir
title: The Mandrake Choir
track: verdant
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(bramble_planted) and not flag(bramble_choir) and spell_level(bramble) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: music
tags: club nature
scene: A row of potted mandrakes in knitted hats screaming in chorus at a nervous seedling, a student with earmuffs approaching with a watering can.
text: The mandrakes in the next bed have taken against your seedling and scream at it in chorus every evening. It's wilting from the noise. Gerald is conducting.
> left: Quiet the choir
  challenge enchant journeyman:
    win:
      flag bramble_choir
      alchemy +small
      say: A drop of valerian in each pot and a firm word with Gerald, and the choir settles into a low hum. Your seedling straightens up and puts out a vine.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: The choir screams at you instead. Your ears ring till supper. Gerald looks unrepentant in his hat.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(verdant_far_bed) >= 1 and flag(bramble_planted) + flag(bramble_fed) + flag(bramble_choir) >= 2:
      queue verdant_bramble_bolts now
    elif not flag(bramble_planted):
      queue verdant_plant_seed now
    elif not flag(bramble_fed):
      queue verdant_cold_snap now
> right: Move the seedling's pot
  mood +tiny
  say: You move it to the quiet end. It perks up, but it's away from the warm pipes now, and it isn't growing.

@event verdant_bramble_bolts
time: night
title: The Night It Bolts
track: verdant
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: tense
when: flag(bramble_chain) and spell_level(bramble) == 0 and since(verdant_far_bed) >= 1 and (flag(bramble_planted) + flag(bramble_fed) + flag(bramble_choir) >= 2 or since(verdant_far_bed) >= 4)
repeat: 2
weight: 40
art: spell_bramble
tags: club nature magic
scene: A greenhouse at night, a thorny hedge surging across the beds toward a row of pale flowers, a student with arms outstretched trying to hold it back.
text: Tobias wakes you at midnight. Your plant has bolted: a hedge of thorns is surging across the greenhouse toward the moonflower beds, and it is not stopping for anyone but you. {flag(bramble_fed) and flag(bramble_choir): It knows your voice.|You're not sure it knows you at all.}
> left: Call it to heel
  challenge enchant adept- +1 if flag(bramble_planted) +1 if flag(bramble_fed) +1 if flag(bramble_choir):
    win:
      learn_spell bramble
      perform verdant +small
      say: You put out your hand and the hedge stops a finger's width from the moonflowers, then folds itself back into your palm like a sleeping cat. Tobias sits down on a bucket and laughs from the belly.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: The thorns take your sleeve and some of your arm before Tobias shears it back. Maud keeps a cutting, and says she'll offer it to you again in Stormbloom.
> right: Wade in and grab the root
  health -small
  challenge enchant adept- likely +1 if flag(bramble_planted) +1 if flag(bramble_fed) +1 if flag(bramble_choir):
    win:
      learn_spell bramble
      perform verdant +small
      say: You wade through thorns to the root and hold it. The hedge goes still, then curls round you instead, gently. You're scratched to ribbons and it's yours.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: You get the root and it gets you. Tobias shears the hedge back by dawn. Maud keeps a cutting for Stormbloom.

# ---------------- Library Assistant → Index (lore) ----------------

@event library_footnote_drawer
title: Footnote's Drawer
track: library_assistant
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: rank(library_assistant) >= 2 and spell_level(index) == 0 and not flag(index_chain) and turn <= 44
repeat: 3
art: cat
tags: job study
scene: A long library catalogue cabinet, a large cat sitting immovably on one drawer, a student crouching to read its label.
text: Footnote has sat on one catalogue drawer for a week and hisses at anyone who comes near it. The label underneath him says OVERDUE, ELEVEN YEARS. The head librarian says whoever finds that book is welcome to the trick of finding books.
> left: Find out what he's guarding
  flag index_chain
  find lead_index
  lore +tiny
  say: You read the card around his tail. A book on wards, borrowed by a Professor Thorne, eleven years ago. Footnote looks at you as if you've finally asked the right question.
  chain_beat = turn
  queue library_fish_footnote now
> right: Shelve around him
  perform library_assistant +tiny
  say: You shelve around Footnote for the rest of the shift. He watches every book you put away, as if marking them.

@event library_fish_footnote
title: Bribing the Cat
track: library_assistant
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(index_chain) and not flag(index_fish) and spell_level(index) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: cat
tags: job
scene: A student offering a small paper parcel of fish to a large, unimpressed cat on a library cabinet.
text: Footnote won't move from the drawer for less than fish. Good fish, from the village, not the refectory's. The head librarian says this is "between you and the cat".
> left: Buy him a proper herring
  gold -small
  flag index_fish
  say: Footnote eats the herring slowly, looking at you the whole time, then steps off the drawer and onto your lap. The card is yours. So, apparently, is the cat.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(library_footnote_drawer) >= 1 and flag(index_fish) + flag(index_hush) + flag(index_string) >= 2:
      queue library_overdue_book now
    elif not flag(index_hush):
      queue library_hush_lamp now
    elif not flag(index_string):
      queue library_wandering_section now
> right: Wait him out
  mood -tiny
  say: You wait. Footnote waits better. At closing he yawns, stretches, and lies back down on the drawer.

@event library_hush_lamp
time: evening
title: The Night Hush
track: library_assistant
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: eerie
when: flag(index_chain) and not flag(index_hush) and spell_level(index) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: lantern
tags: job study
scene: A dark library reading room at night, a student walking the shelves with a lamp held high while the books seem to lean toward the light.
text: The overdue book will only be on the shelves the night hush sends it to. The head librarian lends you the old lamp. "Walk the hush," she says, "and listen to which shelf goes quiet last."
> left: Walk the hush and listen
  challenge research journeyman:
    win:
      flag index_hush
      lore +small
      say: Three laps, and on the third, the shelves on the north side go quiet a heartbeat after the rest. You mark it on your map. The lamp seems pleased with you.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: Every shelf goes quiet at once, which is either very helpful or a joke at your expense. You walk until midnight and mark nothing.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(library_footnote_drawer) >= 1 and flag(index_fish) + flag(index_hush) + flag(index_string) >= 2:
      queue library_overdue_book now
    elif not flag(index_fish):
      queue library_fish_footnote now
    elif not flag(index_string):
      queue library_wandering_section now
> right: Ask the head librarian outright
  perform library_assistant -tiny
  say: "If I told you," she says, "you wouldn't have found it." She gives you extra shelving for asking.

@event library_wandering_section
title: The Wandering Section
track: library_assistant
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(index_chain) and not flag(index_string) and spell_level(index) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: book
tags: job
scene: A student trailing a long ball of string through a maze of library shelves that have visibly rearranged themselves behind them.
text: The section the book belongs to wanders. It was by the stairs on Monday and in the map room on Wednesday. The only way to follow it is to tie a string to the end shelf and walk where it goes, however long that takes.
> left: Follow it with string
  flag index_string
  mood -small
  say: You follow it for six hours, through rooms you didn't know the library had. At the end you know its route by heart and never want to see a ball of string again.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(library_footnote_drawer) >= 1 and flag(index_fish) + flag(index_hush) + flag(index_string) >= 2:
      queue library_overdue_book now
    elif not flag(index_fish):
      queue library_fish_footnote now
    elif not flag(index_hush):
      queue library_hush_lamp now
> right: Wait for it to come back
  lore +tiny
  say: You read at the desk until the section wanders past again, a day later. You learn nothing about its route, and a little about medieval ward-lattices.

@event library_overdue_book
title: Eleven Years Overdue
track: library_assistant
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: eerie
when: flag(index_chain) and spell_level(index) == 0 and since(library_footnote_drawer) >= 1 and (flag(index_fish) + flag(index_hush) + flag(index_string) >= 2 or since(library_footnote_drawer) >= 4)
repeat: 2
weight: 40
art: spell_index
tags: job study magic
scene: A student high on a rolling ladder in a library where the shelves are visibly moving, a cat on their shoulder, one dusty book glowing faintly.
text: Tonight the shelves are moving. Somewhere in the wandering section is the book, eleven years overdue, and every book you touch tries to fall open at the wrong page. {flag(index_fish): Footnote is on your shoulder.|You're on your own.}
> left: Find the page
  challenge research adept- +1 if flag(index_fish) +1 if flag(index_hush) +1 if flag(index_string):
    win:
      learn_spell index
      perform library_assistant +small
      say: Your hand finds the spine before your eyes do, and the book falls open at exactly the page it was borrowed for. Every book you touch afterwards does the same. The head librarian stamps the card, eleven years late, without a word.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: You get lost on the seventh floor among shelves that don't exist by day. Footnote leads you out at dawn, looking smug. The card is still on the drawer.
> right: Pay a senior clerk for their map
  gold -small
  challenge research adept- likely +1 if flag(index_fish) +1 if flag(index_hush) +1 if flag(index_string):
    win:
      learn_spell index
      perform library_assistant +small
      say: The senior clerk's map is ten years out of date and exactly right where it matters. You find the book, and it falls open at the page it was borrowed for. Every book does, after that.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: The map is ten years out of date and mostly wrong. Footnote leads you out at dawn. The book stays lost, for now.

# ---------------- The Gilded Newt → Rapport (charm) ----------------

@event tavern_two_taps
time: evening
title: Two Taps on the Bar
track: tavern
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: rank(tavern) >= 2 and spell_level(rapport) == 0 and not flag(rapport_chain) and turn <= 44
repeat: 3
art: cup
tags: job
scene: A crowded tavern on the edge of a brawl, a landlady tapping the bar twice and the whole room suddenly laughing instead.
text: Two barge-men are halfway out of their chairs when the landlady taps the bar twice, says one sentence you don't catch, and the whole room laughs instead. The fight is over before it began. She catches you staring. "Want to know how?"
> left: "Yes. Teach me."
  flag rapport_chain
  find lead_rapport
  charm +tiny
  say: "Can't teach it," she says. "You earn it. Learn the room, buy the room, work the room." She taps the bar twice at you, and you laugh, and you don't know why.
  chain_beat = turn
  queue tavern_eel_story now
> right: Keep pouring
  perform tavern +tiny
  say: You keep pouring. The barge-men buy each other a drink and sing. The landlady watches you, thoughtfully, for the rest of the shift.

@event tavern_eel_story
time: evening
title: The Eel Story
track: tavern
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(rapport_chain) and not flag(rapport_eel) and spell_level(rapport) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: wave
tags: job
scene: A barge-man at a tavern table with his arms spread wide, telling a story to a student taking notes on a bar napkin.
text: The old barge-man's eel story is the most famous story at the Newt. Regulars mouth along. The landlady says if you can tell it as well as he does, the room will be half yours. He's willing to teach it, slowly, for an evening.
> left: Learn it and tell it back
  challenge perform journeyman wild:
    win:
      flag rapport_eel
      charm +small
      say: You tell it back that same night, to the same corner, and get the laugh at the eel's second escape. The barge-man wipes his eyes and buys you a cider.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: You get the eel's name wrong and the ending backwards. The regulars are very kind about it, which is worse.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(tavern_two_taps) >= 1 and flag(rapport_eel) + flag(rapport_round) + flag(rapport_shift) >= 2:
      queue tavern_festival_room now
    elif not flag(rapport_round):
      queue tavern_regulars_round now
    elif not flag(rapport_shift):
      queue tavern_double_shift now
> right: Just enjoy the story
  mood +small
  say: You sit and listen to the eel story twice through, and laugh both times. You couldn't tell it, but you've rarely had a better evening.

@event tavern_regulars_round
time: evening
title: The Regulars' Corner
track: tavern
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(rapport_chain) and not flag(rapport_round) and spell_level(rapport) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: coin
tags: job
scene: A student setting down a tray of mugs at a crowded corner table in a tavern, the regulars raising them in a toast.
text: The regulars' corner has never had a round bought by staff. The landlady says that's exactly why you should. "Nobody listens to a story from someone who's never stood them a drink."
> left: Stand the corner a round
  gold -small
  flag rapport_round
  say: The corner raises the mugs to you, by name, which you didn't know they knew. For the rest of the night they call you over to settle every argument.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(tavern_two_taps) >= 1 and flag(rapport_eel) + flag(rapport_round) + flag(rapport_shift) >= 2:
      queue tavern_festival_room now
    elif not flag(rapport_eel):
      queue tavern_eel_story now
    elif not flag(rapport_shift):
      queue tavern_double_shift now
> right: Keep your tips
  gold +tiny
  say: You pocket your tips. The corner doesn't notice either way, which is rather the point.

@event tavern_double_shift
title: The Double Shift
track: tavern
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: tense
when: flag(rapport_chain) and not flag(rapport_shift) and spell_level(rapport) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: cup
tags: job
scene: A tired student wiping down a bar at closing time after a very long day, the landlady counting the till beside them.
text: Two servers are down with Lake Fever, and the landlady needs a double shift: lunch through closing. "You'll learn more about a room in fourteen hours," she says, "than in a term of evenings."
> left: Work the double
  wage
  flag rapport_shift
  health -small
  say: Fourteen hours on your feet. By closing you can tell who wants to talk and who wants to be left alone from across the room. Your feet are a separate, angrier person.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(tavern_two_taps) >= 1 and flag(rapport_eel) + flag(rapport_round) + flag(rapport_shift) >= 2:
      queue tavern_festival_room now
    elif not flag(rapport_eel):
      queue tavern_eel_story now
    elif not flag(rapport_round):
      queue tavern_regulars_round now
> right: Turn it down
  perform tavern -tiny
  say: You say you can't. The landlady works it herself, and is short with you for a week.

@event tavern_festival_room
time: evening
title: The Room Is Yours
track: tavern
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: tense
when: flag(rapport_chain) and spell_level(rapport) == 0 and since(tavern_two_taps) >= 1 and (flag(rapport_eel) + flag(rapport_round) + flag(rapport_shift) >= 2 or since(tavern_two_taps) >= 4)
repeat: 2
weight: 40
art: spell_rapport
tags: job magic
scene: A packed tavern on a festival night, a student standing on a chair telling a story while the crowd hangs on every word.
text: The landlady is away for the night and the Newt is packed to the rafters, two barges in and a fight brewing by the fire. It's yours to hold. {flag(rapport_eel) and flag(rapport_round) and flag(rapport_shift): You know this room now.|You know some of this room.}
> left: Tap the bar twice
  challenge negotiate adept- +1 if flag(rapport_eel) +1 if flag(rapport_round) +1 if flag(rapport_shift):
    win:
      learn_spell rapport
      renown +small
      say: You tap the bar twice, say one sentence about an eel, and the room laughs. The fight by the fire turns into a song. When the landlady comes back, she knows at once. She just nods.
    lose:
      gold -small
      say: The tap comes out as a knock and the laugh never comes. A chair breaks, and so do some glasses, and the fine comes out of your wages. Next festival night, she says, you can try again.
> right: Buy the first round, then talk
  gold -small
  challenge negotiate adept- likely +1 if flag(rapport_eel) +1 if flag(rapport_round) +1 if flag(rapport_shift):
    win:
      learn_spell rapport
      renown +small
      say: A round on the house first, then a story while they drink it. By the time the mugs are empty, nobody remembers wanting to fight. The landlady hears about it before she's through the door.
    lose:
      gold -tiny
      say: They drink the round and fight anyway. You mop up with the rest of the staff. Next festival night, the landlady says.

# ---------------- Apothecary Clerk → Distill (alchemy) ----------------

@event pell_oldest_drawer
title: The Oldest Drawer
track: apothecary_clerk
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: eerie
trigger: auto
when: rank(apothecary_clerk) >= 2 and spell_level(purify) == 0 and not flag(distil_chain) and turn <= 44
repeat: 3
art: potion
tags: job
scene: An old apothecary's wall of tiny drawers, one at the very bottom pulled open to reveal a yellowed recipe card, a gruff old man watching from the counter.
text: Restocking, you open the oldest drawer at the bottom of Pell's wall. Inside is one yellowed card: a draught "of your own strength", in a hand older than Pell's. Pell sees it and counts to three under his breath. "That one costs the brewer," he says. "Measure twice."
> left: Copy the recipe
  flag distil_chain
  find lead_distil
  alchemy +tiny
  say: You copy it out carefully. Pell watches you do it and says nothing, then corrects one of your measures in your copy. That is the closest he comes to permission.
  chain_beat = turn
  queue pell_counting_drops now
> right: Close the drawer
  rel pell +tiny
  say: You close it. Pell nods once and goes back to his scales. Later you notice he has relabelled the drawer, clearly, "Not yet."

@event pell_counting_drops
time: night
title: Counting Drops
track: apothecary_clerk
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(distil_chain) and not flag(distil_drops) and spell_level(purify) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: potion
tags: job
scene: A dim apothecary at night, an old man and a student bent over a slowly dripping still, both counting under their breath.
text: Pell distills by the drop, all night, counting aloud. "If you mean to try the old draught," he says, "you'll count with me first. Lose count once and we start again."
> left: Count all night with him
  challenge brew journeyman:
    win:
      flag distil_drops
      alchemy +small
      say: Four hundred and twelve drops, and you don't lose count once. At dawn Pell says "Fair," which is once a decade, and lets you stopper the bottle.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: You lose count at three hundred and something. Pell starts again without comment. So do you. You lose it again.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(pell_oldest_drawer) >= 1 and flag(distil_drops) + flag(distil_moonwort) + flag(distil_shortcut) >= 2:
      queue pell_draught now
    elif not flag(distil_moonwort):
      queue pell_buy_moonwort now
    elif not flag(distil_shortcut):
      queue pell_daughters_shortcut now
> right: Go home and sleep
  health +tiny
  say: You go home. Pell counts on alone, steadily, through the night. In the morning the bottle is full and labelled, and he says nothing about it.

@event pell_buy_moonwort
title: Moonwort
track: apothecary_clerk
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(distil_chain) and not flag(distil_moonwort) and spell_level(purify) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: leaf
tags: job
scene: An apothecary counter with a small jar labelled "Moonwort. Do not hum near.", a student counting out coins beside it.
text: The old draught needs moonwort, and the only good moonwort in the village is the jar on Pell's top shelf, labelled "Do not hum near." Pell sells it to staff at cost. The cost is not small.
> left: Buy the moonwort
  gold -small
  flag distil_moonwort
  say: Pell weighs it twice and wraps it in waxed paper. You carry it home without humming, which is harder than it sounds.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(pell_oldest_drawer) >= 1 and flag(distil_drops) + flag(distil_moonwort) + flag(distil_shortcut) >= 2:
      queue pell_draught now
    elif not flag(distil_drops):
      queue pell_counting_drops now
    elif not flag(distil_shortcut):
      queue pell_daughters_shortcut now
> right: Try the cheap substitute
  mood -tiny
  say: The substitute smells wrong the moment you open it. Pell takes it from you without a word and puts it in the bin.

@event pell_daughters_shortcut
title: The Daughters' Shortcut
track: apothecary_clerk
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: tense
when: flag(distil_chain) and not flag(distil_shortcut) and spell_level(purify) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: potion
tags: job
scene: The back room of an apothecary, a student drinking a small cup of something dark while two women watch with professional interest.
text: Pell's daughters say there's a shortcut: learn what the draught takes out of a brewer by tasting a little of it first. "Father hates it," says one. "It works," says the other. "You'll be ill for a day."
> left: Try it on yourself
  flag distil_shortcut
  health -small
  say: It takes the strength out of your knees and then, slowly, gives it back. You spend a day in bed. When you get up, you know exactly where the draught will pull from.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(pell_oldest_drawer) >= 1 and flag(distil_drops) + flag(distil_moonwort) + flag(distil_shortcut) >= 2:
      queue pell_draught now
    elif not flag(distil_drops):
      queue pell_counting_drops now
    elif not flag(distil_moonwort):
      queue pell_buy_moonwort now
> right: Do it Pell's way
  rel pell +tiny
  say: You decline. The daughters shrug. Pell, who was listening, corrects a label more firmly than it needed.

@event pell_draught
title: Of Your Own Strength
track: apothecary_clerk
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: eerie
when: flag(distil_chain) and spell_level(purify) == 0 and since(pell_oldest_drawer) >= 1 and (flag(distil_drops) + flag(distil_moonwort) + flag(distil_shortcut) >= 2 or since(pell_oldest_drawer) >= 4)
repeat: 2
weight: 40
art: spell_distil
tags: job magic
scene: An apothecary's still at night, a student drawing a single shining drop out of a dark mixture while an old man holds the lamp.
text: Pell closes the shop early, sets the old still on the bench and holds the lamp himself. "Brew it," he says. "I'll count." The recipe card lies beside you. {flag(distil_drops) and flag(distil_moonwort) and flag(distil_shortcut): You know every step of it.|There are steps you haven't practised.}
> left: Brew the draught
  challenge brew adept- +1 if flag(distil_drops) +1 if flag(distil_moonwort) +1 if flag(distil_shortcut):
    win:
      learn_spell purify
      perform apothecary_clerk +small
      say: The draught comes down to one shining drop, and as it falls you feel exactly what it took from you, and how to take it again. Pell stops counting. "Fair," he says, twice in one year.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: The mixture boils over and takes more out of you than it should. Pell puts the card back in the drawer and writes "Don't." on the front. Next term, perhaps.
> right: Use Pell's own moonwort stock
  gold -small
  challenge brew adept- likely +1 if flag(distil_drops) +1 if flag(distil_moonwort) +1 if flag(distil_shortcut):
    win:
      learn_spell purify
      perform apothecary_clerk +small
      say: With the good stock, it comes down clean to one drop. You feel it pull, and you feel where it pulls from. Pell writes the cost in his ledger, and your name beside the recipe.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: Even with his best stock it boils over. Pell writes "Don't." on the drawer and the cost in the ledger. Next term, perhaps.

# ---------------- Broom Courier → Tailwind (vigor) ----------------

@event courier_wind_jar
title: Wind in a Jar
track: broom_courier
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: rank(broom_courier) >= 2 and spell_level(tailwind) == 0 and not flag(tailwind_chain) and turn <= 44
repeat: 3
art: broom
tags: job
scene: A courier loft with a dusty shelf of unclaimed letters, a student holding up a stoppered jar in which a small wind is visibly whirling.
text: On the dead-letter shelf, behind a parcel addressed to nobody, is a stoppered jar with a wind in it, going round and round. The label says FOR WHOEVER IS FAST ENOUGH. The loft master says someone flew with it once, before her time.
> left: Take the jar down
  flag tailwind_chain
  find lead_tailwind
  vigor +tiny
  say: The jar hums in your hands, and every broom in the loft leans toward you. The loft master writes your name on the jar's label, under a name too faded to read.
  chain_beat = turn
  queue courier_fisherman_waves now
> right: Leave it on the shelf
  perform broom_courier +tiny
  say: You leave it for whoever is fast enough. You fly your round. The jar's wind stirs the dead letters as you go.

@event courier_fisherman_waves
title: The Fisherman Waves
track: broom_courier
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: warm
when: flag(tailwind_chain) and not flag(tailwind_fisherman) and spell_level(tailwind) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: wave
tags: job
scene: An old fisherman in a small boat on a grey lake waving up at a student on a broom flying low overhead.
text: The old fisherman in the reed beds has never waved at a courier. Today, seeing the jar strapped to your broom, he waves, and beckons you down. "That jar," he says. "I flew it once. Fastest year of my life."
> left: Land and ask him about it
  challenge appeal journeyman:
    win:
      flag tailwind_fisherman
      charm +small
      say: He tells you, slowly, between casts: you don't fly the wind, you let it get behind you and keep going. Never stop. "Stopping's what kills it," he says, and goes back to his line.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: He talks about fish for an hour, then says the light's going, and rows off. You'll have to come back.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(courier_wind_jar) >= 1 and flag(tailwind_fisherman) + flag(tailwind_gulls) + flag(tailwind_broom) >= 2:
      queue courier_storm_delivery now
    elif not flag(tailwind_gulls):
      queue courier_race_gulls now
    elif not flag(tailwind_broom):
      queue courier_fix_broom now
> right: Wave back and fly on
  perform broom_courier +small
  say: You wave and fly on with your round, on time. He watches you go, and doesn't wave again.

@event courier_race_gulls
title: Racing the Gulls
track: broom_courier
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(tailwind_chain) and not flag(tailwind_gulls) and spell_level(tailwind) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: broom
tags: job
scene: A student on a broom flying flat out over a lake in a cloud of wheeling gulls, letters fluttering in a satchel.
text: The gulls over the lake race couriers for fun. The fisherman says the jar's wind won't follow you until you've beaten them once, flat out, from the jetty to the far bank.
> left: Race them flat out
  challenge feat journeyman wild:
    win:
      flag tailwind_gulls
      vigor +small
      say: You hit the far bank a beak ahead of the lead gull. The wind in the jar turns over once, like a cat settling. The gulls follow you home, offended.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: You clip a wave at full speed and skip across the lake like a stone. The gulls are delighted. You are wet to the bone.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(courier_wind_jar) >= 1 and flag(tailwind_fisherman) + flag(tailwind_gulls) + flag(tailwind_broom) >= 2:
      queue courier_storm_delivery now
    elif not flag(tailwind_fisherman):
      queue courier_fisherman_waves now
    elif not flag(tailwind_broom):
      queue courier_fix_broom now
> right: Fly your round steady
  perform broom_courier +tiny
  say: You fly the round steady and deliver everything dry. The gulls lose interest. So does the jar.

@event courier_fix_broom
title: The Broom That Pulls Left
track: broom_courier
rank: 2
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(tailwind_chain) and not flag(tailwind_broom) and spell_level(tailwind) == 0
repeat: 2
weight: 60
art: broom
tags: job
scene: A broom-maker's bench in the village, a craftsman sighting along a broom handle while a student waits with their satchel.
text: Your loft broom pulls left, always has. With the jar's wind behind it, it would pull you into the lake. The broom-maker in the village can true it, for a price.
> left: Pay to have it trued
  gold -small
  flag tailwind_broom
  say: The broom-maker sights along it, tuts, and spends an afternoon on it. It flies straight for the first time in living memory. You miss the pull, a little.
  if chain_beat != turn:
    chain_beat = turn
    if since(courier_wind_jar) >= 1 and flag(tailwind_fisherman) + flag(tailwind_gulls) + flag(tailwind_broom) >= 2:
      queue courier_storm_delivery now
    elif not flag(tailwind_fisherman):
      queue courier_fisherman_waves now
    elif not flag(tailwind_gulls):
      queue courier_race_gulls now
> right: Learn to fly it crooked
  mood -tiny
  say: You learn to lean right all the time. Your back complains, and the broom keeps pulling left out of habit.

@event courier_storm_delivery
title: The Storm Run
track: broom_courier
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: tense
when: flag(tailwind_chain) and spell_level(tailwind) == 0 and since(courier_wind_jar) >= 1 and (flag(tailwind_fisherman) + flag(tailwind_gulls) + flag(tailwind_broom) >= 2 or since(courier_wind_jar) >= 4)
repeat: 2
weight: 40
art: spell_tailwind
tags: job magic
scene: A student on a broom flying through a storm over a dark lake, a jar of wind unstoppered at their belt, lightning behind them.
text: A storm is down on the lake, and a parcel must cross it tonight. The loft master looks at the jar at your belt, then at you. "Nobody else will go," she says. {flag(tailwind_fisherman) and flag(tailwind_gulls) and flag(tailwind_broom): You know how to let the wind get behind you.|You've never flown it in weather.}
> left: Open the jar and go
  challenge feat adept- +1 if flag(tailwind_fisherman) +1 if flag(tailwind_gulls) +1 if flag(tailwind_broom):
    win:
      learn_spell tailwind
      perform broom_courier +small
      say: You pull the stopper and the wind gets behind you and doesn't stop. You cross the lake faster than the lightning can find you. The parcel arrives dry. The wind stays with you after, when you call it.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: Halfway across, a gust takes you and you ditch in the shallows. The parcel survives. You barely do. The next storm season, the loft master says, you can try again.
> right: Wait for the lull, then go
  mood -small
  challenge feat adept- likely +1 if flag(tailwind_fisherman) +1 if flag(tailwind_gulls) +1 if flag(tailwind_broom):
    win:
      learn_spell tailwind
      perform broom_courier +small
      say: You wait, nerves screaming, for the gap in the storm, then open the jar and go. The wind gets behind you and stays. The parcel arrives an hour late and dry, and the wind is yours.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: The lull never comes, and you go anyway and ditch in the shallows. The next storm season, the loft master says.
